{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00012","versions":[{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00012","release":"R19-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00012","release":"R20-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00012","release":"R21-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00012","release":"R22-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00012@rel:R23-11#06d6745a","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00012","release":"R23-11","content":"[SWS_SecOC_00012] ⌈\nIf the SecOC module uses the Csm module asynchronously to calculate or verify the\nauthenticator, SecOC shall provide adequate callback functions for every CsmJob to\nget notification about the result of the asynchronous job.\n⌋ (SRS_BSW_00457, SRS_SecOC_00003)\nNote: CSM jobs can run synchronously or asynchronously, which depends on its configuration. For\nasynchronous jobs a callback is needed to get notified when the operation is finished. This callback is\nnot defined in this document. They are vendor specific and shall be configured accordingly in the CSM\nas documented in [SWS_Csm_00971].","meta":{"source_pdf":"SWS_SecureOnboardCommunication.pdf","source_page":78,"trigger_kind":"snippet_ingest"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-04T00:00:00+00:00"},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00012","release":"R24-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00012","release":"R25-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTO